@startuml 4_1_Game_StateMachine
' MyBattleship -- GroupXXAssign2.pdf, section 4.1: Game (state diagram)
' Models the Game class lifecycle (GameState enum). InProgress is expanded in section 4.4.
title MyBattleship -- Game Lifecycle (State Machine)

hide empty description
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 75
skinparam padding 5
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam StateFontSize 14
skinparam StateAttributeFontSize 12
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
  ArrowColor Black
}

[*] --> Placement : addPlayer(p)\n[lobby seats == 2]\n/ create empty Boards

state Placement : entry / both players given 5 ships
state Placement : do / await confirmPlacement()

state InProgress <<composite>> : entry / beginBattle(), currentTurn chosen at random
state InProgress : do / turn cycle, expanded in section 4.4 (Turn Cycle)

state Finished : entry / declareWinner(p, endReason), finishedAt = now
state Finished : do / hold RematchRequest

Placement --> Placement : confirmPlacement()\n[one player isReady, other not]\n/ show waiting state
Placement --> Placement : placeShips(layout)\n[not canPlace(...)]\n/ return PlacementError
Placement --> InProgress : confirmPlacement()\n[both players isReady and server re-validated]\n/ turnStartedAt = now
Placement --> Finished : claimTimeout(code)\n[opponent gone > 60 s during placement]\n/ declareWinner(OPPONENT_DISCONNECTED)

InProgress --> Finished : shotResolved\n[allShipsSunk() on either Board]\n/ declareWinner(FLEET_DESTROYED)
InProgress --> Finished : forfeit(p)\n[player selects Forfeit]\n/ declareWinner(OPPONENT_FORFEIT)
InProgress --> Finished : claimTimeout(code)\n[opponent gone > 60 s]\n/ declareWinner(OPPONENT_DISCONNECTED)

Finished --> Placement : requestRematch(code, true)\n[isMutual()]\n/ Lobby.reset(): empty Boards, new Game in same Lobby
Finished --> [*] : requestRematch(code, false)\n[declined, or a player left]\n/ lobby abandoned

note bottom of InProgress
  Composite state. Its sub-states, events and
  guards are shown in section 4.4 (Turn Cycle).
end note
@enduml
